From 43c7a5c129734ab0b1a5c2d1c421e0f7651e110b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CounterStrikeXB2 <cs2@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: model the MCPX Ethernet controller; frames over UDP
 (CounterStrikeXB2 local patch)

nvnet.c answers the NIC registers at 0xFEF00000 (trapped, as OHCI), walks the TX/RX descriptor rings and raises the NIC interrupt to the title's ISR, so XNet runs unmodified. nvnet_link.c carries each Ethernet frame in a UDP datagram (port 30740) to every interface's broadcast address and RECOMP_NET_PEERS, making running instances on a LAN one segment for system link. The NIC answers XNet's DHCP itself (169.254.x.y/16 from the MAC) so map loads do not wait out the DHCP timeout. XC_FACTORY_ETHERNET_ADDR returns the NIC's MAC (RECOMP_XBOX_MAC, else from the computer name). Off unless RECOMP_NET=1.
